## Maps Code Assist — required workflow

**Server names:** upstream docs say `gmp-code-assist`; in Cursor this repo configures **`google-maps-code-assist`** → same URL `https://mapscodeassist.googleapis.com/mcp` (may appear as `user-google-maps-code-assist` in the UI).

**Auto-use MCP** when the task mentions: maps/pins, geocoding, Places/Routes, Street View, POI, store locator, routing, logistics, Medellín neighborhoods, field masks, `mapId`, AdvancedMarker, Grounding Lite, or any MAP-### task.

Before **any** GMP implementation or task spec change (Places, Routes, vis.gl, Advanced Markers, grounding):

1. Call MCP **`retrieve-instructions`** with `{ "name": "instructions" }` — **always first** ([tool schema](https://developers.google.com/maps/ai/code-assist/reference/mcp/tools_list/retrieve-instructions))
2. Call **`retrieve-google-maps-platform-docs`** with a concrete `llmQuery` + optional `filter` (e.g. `"Places API (New)"`, `"field mask"`, `"Advanced Markers"`)
3. Ground every API name, field mask, and `mapId` claim in code — **do not** rely on training data alone
4. **Validate:** `cd mdeapp && npm test` / `npm run floor` after code changes; cite doc URI in task evidence when flipping MAP Done

Set `source: "mdeai-app"` (≤64 chars) on doc queries for analytics.

**Attribution:** When presenting MCP doc results to users, include Google Maps source links from `documentationUri`.

**ToS:** Do not cache MCP doc payloads for model training; product DB rules for `generativeSummary` are separate (see skill).

**Deprecated path:** Do **not** add npm `@googlemaps/code-assist-mcp` — [platform-ai README](https://github.com/googlemaps/platform-ai) deprecates npm by **2026-07-01**; use **hosted HTTP MCP** only.

